WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.980
This is Masara Town.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.360
And here lives...

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:21.620
Mom!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.960
I can go too, can't I?

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.330
To Professor Okido's Pokémon Camp!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.630
It's a camp to observe wild Pokémon
with Professor Okido!

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.590
Huh, a camp to observe wild Pokémon?

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.550
All right, I'll sign you up.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.100
Yay! All right!

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.400
But I have things to do
that morning.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.060
You'll have to get up
on your own.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.610
I can't wait!

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.860
Satoshi, are you listening?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.860
I wonder what kind
of Pokémon I'll meet!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.660
Pocket Monsters...

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.870
Pokémon for short.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.830
Strange, strange creatures
with countless secrets.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:09.710
Some Pokémon live happily
alongside humans...

00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:12.920
But in the grass...

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.640
In the air...

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.640
and in the water,
you'll find wild Pokémon, too!

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.980
And in this forest...

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.360
Pichu is a Pokémon who can
discharge electricity.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.450
It still can't use it well, though.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:52.730
There are many Pokémon
who live in packs in the forest,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.730
but it appears that
this Pichu is all alone.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:55.410
The lonely Pichu...

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:58.710
...began living with the Garura family.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:02.270
Several weeks later...

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.780
...the day had come
for Professor Okido's camp.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:14.990
Professor Okido!
Aren't we leaving yet?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:18.620
Well, you see...
There's supposed to be one more coming.

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:22.120
The meetup time's
already over, though...

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.380
He's an energetic little boy
who lives nearby...

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:30.670
Probably went "I'm going on a trip tomorrow,
so I'm too excited to sleep!"

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:33.680
I bet he's careless and simple-minded.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:39.890
Can't wait...
for the Pokémon... Camp...

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.850
That does describe him pretty well...

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.110
But, um... Who are you?

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:47.690
I'm Go!
She invited me here!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.230
Oh, you're Koharu's friend?

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:53.740
That's right! Go comes to play
at Dad's lab all the time!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.740
Is Professor Sakuragi
doing all right?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:57.740
Yes!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:01.000
Koharu's father is
a Pokémon researcher, as well.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:06.750
He shows great promise, as well;
He's been deemed a genius since he was young.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:11.130
So, how long are we gonna wait
for the careless and simple-minded guy?

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:14.640
We don't want to be late <i>back</i>, either...

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:17.260
Oh, well. I guess we're setting off.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.520
The... sun?!

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.270
Professor Okido! Everyone!
Wait for me!

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:34.700
All right, it's time to explore the forest
and observe the Pokémon living here!

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.070
<i>All right!</i>

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:44.370
A real live Caterpie!

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.590
Go, Monster Ball!

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.480
All right! I got Caterpie!

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:09.570
As you just saw, you can catch wild Pokémon
by throwing Monster Balls at them.

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:14.030
When you turn ten,
you can become Pokémon Trainers,

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:16.490
get your own starter Pokémon,

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.990
and embark on an adventure
with Pokémon!

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.870
But before that, you should get yourselves
plenty of Pokémon knowledge!

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.130
<i>All right! We got it!</i>

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:33.420
I've already got more Pokémon knowledge
than I'll ever need, though!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.210
Go?!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:36.670
That's great to hear!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.310
Do you know what this Pokémon is?

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:50.650
It's Cocoon,
the Cocoon Pokémon, yeah?

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:52.520
Oh! Correct!

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:54.990
Well, do you know
that Pokémon, then?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.030
That's Kamonegi, yeah?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.740
The thing in its mouth is a plant stalk.
The stalk is used like a sword to cut all sorts of things!

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.120
Amazing!

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:04.120
Awesome!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.620
I can't believe you knew that!

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.250
That's Digda! A Pokémon that
feeds on plant roots!

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:11.920
Here's Digda's evolved form; Dugtrio!

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:19.430
It's amazingly strong!
It can dig to a depth of 100 kilometers!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:23.390
Go! <i>Professor Okido</i> is supposed to
provide the Pokémon explanations!

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:27.600
You really <i>do</i> know a lot about Pokémon,
don't you, Go?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:33.480
Just like Go just said,
Pokémon evolve.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.980
The conditions for them to evolve vary,

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:39.150
but Pokémon are creatures who
change their appearance and shape.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.160
But Kamonegi don't evolve!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.160
T-That's right...

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:50.170
Not every Pokémon evolves!
But some Pokémon do, right?

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.120
Go!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:53.420
It's quite all right.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:59.840
Now let's look at the Pokémon
living in the water.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.300
Come on, Go!

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.510
This is why you can't make any friends!

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:07.270
I don't want to get <i>friends</i>...

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:12.480
I want to get an amazing Pokémon someday!
One that nobody's ever seen!

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.150
Hey, are you mocking me?!

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.190
I mean, that's just a dream...

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.110
It's not a dream! It's the future!

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:23.240
And that future lies in my hands!

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.160
Huh?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.500
It's a Nidoking!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:31.790
Huh?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:42.220
It vanished?!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.600
No way!

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:04.450
It used the same move as Nidoking!

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.720
The same move again?!

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:38.190
It's playing by using
the same moves as its opponent!

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:44.030
Who's that Pokémon?!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.830
Go, wait!

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:58.670
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.890
Go! I said wait!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.140
Where'd that Pokémon go?!

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.140
Oh, come on, Go!

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:17.940
Boobur!

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:24.240
Go!

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.280
It turned into a Kentauros?!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.000
And now a Laplace?!

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.460
I'm not giving up!

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.960
Go!

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:50.890
Meanwhile, in the same forest,
Pichu had become good friends with the Garura family...

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.190
These Pokémon are called Lucky.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.700
They'll share their eggs
with their friends.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:13.200
Lucky's eggs are highly nutritious,
and the Pokémon love them.

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:33.140
I'm sure it flew this way...

00:14:33.140 --> 00:14:35.930
Go, let's go back to the others.

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:38.560
I'm sure Professor Okido is worried!

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.930
Oh, no!

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.260
Professor Okido!

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:40.640
Oh, there you are!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.230
I looked all over for you!

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.190
That might have been Mew.

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:50.230
Mew?

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:53.370
It's said to live deep in the jungle...

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:58.790
But since it can freely hide itself,
it's very hard to spot.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:01.750
It seems to contain
the genes of every Pokémon.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.710
It's known as a Mythical Pokémon.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.580
A Mythical Pokémon?

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:09.920
Awesome... Mew is amazing!

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:14.170
I wanna turn ten already!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:17.390
Turn ten, become a Pokémon Trainer...

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.810
Then I'll catch that Pokémon...
I'll catch Mew, for sure!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.230
A new meeting...

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:30.230
A small missed opportunity...

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.570
Then, some time later...

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:49.540
Pichu and Garura's child
had both grown a bit bigger.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:33.250
One parting...

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:36.080
...leads to another meeting.

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:39.170
Several years later...

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:45.390
Satoshi, the young boy who
lives in Masara Town...

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:47.010
...had turned ten.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:53.430
The... sun?!

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:57.400
On the day he was finally set to embark
on his journey as a Pokémon Trainer,

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.070
Satoshi overslept again,

00:21:01.480 --> 00:21:04.530
but he was still able to
get his first Pokémon.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:17.330
It's called Pikachu.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.130
So cute! He's perfect!

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:20.880
Really?

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.460
Yeah!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.470
Pikachu, it's so nice to meet you!

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:27.550
What's...

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:29.470
It's also known as
the electric mouse.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.020
It's quite shy,
and doesn't take to people very well.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:34.060
This is what happens if
you touch it carelessly.

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:37.440
Pikachu, huh?

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:39.730
I'm Satoshi! Nice to meet you!

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:43.940
This meeting was the start of
Satoshi and Pikachu's story.

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.360
The two have shared
many adventures,

00:21:47.360 --> 00:21:50.740
and now the curtain rises
on yet another one!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.510
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:05.100
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:07.800
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:10.680
And skip the slow send-off

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:13.010
Be it through fire or through water

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:15.680
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:20.200
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:25.440
Each and every one of my memories

00:22:25.440 --> 00:22:30.040
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:22:31.200 --> 00:22:33.950
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:39.710
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:22:41.670 --> 00:22:46.710
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:50.800
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:52.260
Let's have a fight!

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:54.970
1: Once the battle's done

00:22:54.970 --> 00:22:56.810
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:22:56.810 --> 00:23:01.150
On 3, let's be friends!

00:23:02.450 --> 00:23:07.820
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:13.160
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:15.660
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:19.790
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:21.500
I choose you!

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:32.220
Oh, yeah... Go hardly ever
goes to school, right?

00:23:32.680 --> 00:23:34.100
That's right...

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:38.850
It's like researching and observing
Pokémon is <i>all</i> he ever does.

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:52.110
The future...

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:54.030
...already...

00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:56.870
...lies in my hands!

00:24:01.910 --> 00:24:04.250
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:05.880
Go!

00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:11.920
An exceedingly rare Pokémon
will show itself at Kuchiba Port!

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:13.890
What?! Lugia?!

00:24:13.890 --> 00:24:15.510
Let's all fight together!

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:16.440
It's a Raid Battle!

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:17.640
Wait!

00:24:17.640 --> 00:24:19.390
I'll be the one to battle Lugia!

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:21.810
No! The future lies in <i>my</i> hands!

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:22.690
Who are you?!

00:24:22.690 --> 00:24:24.440
Right back at you!

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:26.400
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:
Aboard Lugia They Go!
Satoshi and Go,

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:29.030
Satoshi and Go, Aboard Lugia They Go!
Aboard Lugia They Go!
Satoshi and Go,

00:24:29.030 --> 00:24:30.450
Aboard Lugia They Go!
Satoshi and Go,
